Build-host paths
----------------

`libksud.so` embeds a build-user cargo-registry path (`…/.cargo/registry/…`)
from the machine that built it. The binary is otherwise unmodified from the
repository artifact. Rebuild with `RUSTFLAGS="--remap-path-prefix=$HOME=/build"`
to strip such paths in future refreshes.

LKM (`dfroot.ko`)
-----------------

The LKM binary is intentionally NOT committed. It is built from
`lkm/dfroot.c` (GPL-2.0-only, `MODULE_LICENSE("GPL")`) by the top-level
`Makefile` (one podman build for the single KMI `android13-5.15`, using the
digest-pinned image
`ghcr.io/ylarod/ddk-min:android13-5.15-20260828@sha256:9e68cd9fcab748584755d31ba88ef134efc938dbde17f258c2652315f6cd81cd`
resolved via `scripts/ddk-image.sh`) or by CI
(`.github/workflows/build.yml`), and copied to
`app/src/main/jni/ko/dfroot-android13-5.15.ko` (all `*.ko` under that directory
are gitignored). CI strips `.note.gnu.build-id`, so the CI/release artifact
(13,384 B, sha256
`9dfb8b71b306f5a38fd8b35b283d4dab8b4eb25a08ad97ca0f4ef705b6151c68`) is not
byte-identical to the local `make` build (13,504 B, sha256 `94f8be98…`, which
retains the build-id note). Fresh clones must run the LKM build
(or download CI artifacts) before `assembleRelease`; see README.md and
PORTING-GZIF.md §8.

Validation status and release gates
-----------------------------------

The run6/run8 hardware results recorded in `PORTING-GZIF.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`
(2026-11-17) belong to the **historical implementation only**: the old
multi-marker status protocol, the then-current `dfroot.ko` pins and the old
preference-write path. The current round-2 PR #3 changes (single `/dev/dffinal`
outcome, KO hash-skip policy, build provenance, Java preference persistence)
are **host-tested only and UNVALIDATED on device**. The round-3 phase-2 build
and packaging gates and the phase-3 Java launch/boot gating described below are
likewise host-tested only (the 15 JVM tests run without an Android runtime).

- **No release with obsolete KO pins.** If a DDK rebuild no longer matches the
  two reviewed SHA-256 pins in `app/src/main/jni/CMakeLists.txt`, stop and
  verify out of band; update pins in a reviewed commit or do not release. Skip
  mode is forbidden in CI/release builds. Gradle passes the Android variant
  (`release` / `debug`) as the authoritative native policy signal.
- **Final packaged bytes (no skip).** The KO is linked into a dedicated
  `.dfroot_ko` section; `verify_packaged_ko.cmake` dumps it from
  `libdfroot.so` with objcopy and compares it to the SAME reviewed pins and
  expected sizes. Configure fails without `CMAKE_OBJCOPY`; the gate has no
  skip option and writes a manifest only on success. Tag CI repeats it on the
  real APK before upload. **This real gate is blocked until KO re-pin**: the
  final embedded bytes must be reviewed and deliberately re-pinned before a
  tag can ship. Host-only fixture tests are not device validation.
- **Provenance is evidence, not proof or attestation.** The build/provenance
  manifests record hashes, toolchain identity, git HEAD, Android variant and
  KO gate status for auditing, and fail closed on a missing/stale KO manifest;
  they are not an independent reproducible-build proof, and splicehelper is
  not claimed to be bit-for-bit deterministic across toolchains.
- **All CI suites are asserted.** Every native/CMake/JVM suite writes a marker
  that CI checks, the JUnit XML must report 15 tests with 0 failures/errors, and
  a release-evidence step cross-checks git SHA, skip OFF in every CMakeCache,
  verified KO and packaged manifests with the same hash, and the APK hash.
  Only the informational provenance uploads remain best-effort.
- **Phase 3 Java gates (host-only).** `PreferenceIntegrity.java` quarantines a
  failed SharedPreferences write in memory and on disk (durable marker in
  device-protected storage, same-key recovery, fail closed on marker I/O error).
  `ExploitRunner` returns rc 9 for `/dev/df` and rc 8 for uncertain preferences;
  `StatusRc` maps rc 0–9 plus the additive 64 recovery bit truthfully. No device
  run has exercised these paths; they are not a substitute for on-device
  validation.
- **Auto Soft Reboot / Start on Boot remain disabled by default and
  unvalidated** on S9180ZHU8GZIF.
- **P1-08 release gate — still OPEN.** The bundled loaders hardcode
  `/data/local/tmp/.ksud-stage`; race-at-creation is fixed, but a `shell`-uid
  process could still swap the staged file before the loader renames it. This
  cannot be closed without rebuilding the loaders and is a release gate.
  Phase 3 only documents the Java-side gating; documenting a gate is not a fix.

